Da-rae, do you want more abalone?

279
00:17:44,523 --> 00:17:45,274
This one?

280
00:17:45,858 --> 00:17:46,775
No?

281
00:17:51,488 --> 00:17:54,283
What's happening
with Aunt Yi-gyeong?

282
00:17:56,076 --> 00:17:57,161
Mom and Dad

283
00:17:57,578 --> 00:17:58,579
will make sure

284
00:17:59,079 --> 00:18:00,372
she isn't affected

285
00:18:01,540 --> 00:18:02,666
and take responsibility.

286
00:18:07,838 --> 00:18:13,594
I haven't forgiven you.
I'll be watching, so keep your promise.

287
00:18:17,431 --> 00:18:23,604
I believed...
my mom and dad were good people...

288
00:18:26,065 --> 00:18:29,777
I just hope you stop disappointing me.

289
00:18:31,528 --> 00:18:33,321
I won't

290
00:18:33,322 --> 00:18:34,490
let you down.

291
00:18:36,158 --> 00:18:39,369
Da-rae, for you too,

292
00:18:39,370 --> 00:18:41,120
in the future,

293
00:18:41,121 --> 00:18:43,414
if you have worries,

294
00:18:43,415 --> 00:18:44,958
we hope you will tell

295
00:18:46,251 --> 00:18:48,170
Mom and Dad first.

296
00:18:49,213 --> 00:18:49,963
Okay?

297
00:18:54,968 --> 00:18:56,094
Da-rae?

298
00:18:56,095 --> 00:18:57,096
Let's eat.

299
00:18:57,763 --> 00:19:00,224
This is really delicious, isn't it?

300
00:19:05,396 --> 00:19:07,689
Oh, right. After I'm done eating,

301
00:19:07,690 --> 00:19:09,274
I'll just go check on
the building for a bit.

302
00:19:09,525 --> 00:19:11,777
Because of that fire,
I have so much to take care of.

303
00:19:20,327 --> 00:19:21,786
You're going to find

304
00:19:21,787 --> 00:19:22,829
Yi-gyeong's phone, right?

305
00:19:22,830 --> 00:19:25,790
Yes, if they find that phone,
we'll be caught.

306
00:19:25,791 --> 00:19:27,334
I don't think it's been found yet.

307
00:19:29,586 --> 00:19:31,046
I swear, there's no other meaning.

308
00:19:32,089 --> 00:19:34,174
We need to make sure we don't
get caught so we can protect Yi-gyeong.

309
00:19:38,053 --> 00:19:39,637
I'll go too.

310
00:19:39,638 --> 00:19:41,265
No, I'll go alone.

311
00:19:41,598 --> 00:19:43,642
You shouldn't get mixed up in this.

312
00:19:44,143 --> 00:19:46,854
Well, it's nice of you to care so early.

313
00:19:47,938 --> 00:19:49,523
Okay, fine.

314
00:20:09,585 --> 00:20:10,836
Are you okay?

315
00:20:12,546 --> 00:20:14,548
No, not really.

316
00:20:17,551 --> 00:20:18,385
Let's go check.

317
00:20:28,812 --> 00:20:31,482
It seems like the phone isn't here.

318
00:20:32,107 --> 00:20:34,735
I've searched everywhere.
I really can't find it.

319
00:20:36,028 --> 00:20:37,946
The police didn't find it first, did they?

320
00:20:39,740 --> 00:20:41,116
I hope not.

321
00:20:46,914 --> 00:20:48,499
Jeez...

322
00:20:50,083 --> 00:20:51,375
Actually,

323
00:20:51,376 --> 00:20:52,878
I got a divorce consultation.

324
00:20:53,754 --> 00:20:55,297
To get a divorce with you.

325
00:20:57,800 --> 00:20:58,717
All of a sudden?

326
00:20:59,927 --> 00:21:01,011
Are you serious?

327
00:21:01,386 --> 00:21:02,387
I mean it.

328
00:21:04,389 --> 00:21:06,809
Ever since
you bought this building, well...

329
00:21:08,227 --> 00:21:10,979
Da-rae keeps growing
and I have so much to do,

330
00:21:11,897 --> 00:21:14,191
but I have to handle all that alone.

331
00:21:15,984 --> 00:21:18,862
You're too busy being a landlord,

332
00:21:19,655 --> 00:21:21,657
not even caring about Da-rae and me.

333
00:21:22,199 --> 00:21:23,283
So, I figured

334
00:21:23,784 --> 00:21:26,494
let's just hold on
until Da-rae goes to college.

335
00:21:26,495 --> 00:21:28,622
I think that's how I've been
getting through each day.

336
00:21:29,873 --> 00:21:30,999
Oh,

337
00:21:32,084 --> 00:21:34,253
what are you even saying?

338
00:21:35,212 --> 00:21:36,004
Hey,

339
00:21:36,338 --> 00:21:37,881
people all live like that.

340
00:21:39,091 --> 00:21:40,467
You're just saying that, right?

341
00:21:41,260 --> 00:21:42,093
No.

342
00:21:42,094 --> 00:21:43,470
It's not just talk.

343
00:21:44,054 --> 00:21:45,722
Hey, come on.

344
00:21:47,182 --> 00:21:48,559
So you all are here?

345
00:21:50,727 --> 00:21:53,063
It's a relief there wasn't
too much damage.

346
00:21:53,355 --> 00:21:54,105
Yes.

347
00:21:54,106 --> 00:21:55,732
It could have been worse.

348
00:21:55,983 --> 00:21:57,234
But what brings you here?

349
00:21:57,860 --> 00:21:58,610
Oh.

350
00:21:59,194 --> 00:22:00,821
I just wanted to ask something.

351
00:22:01,655 --> 00:22:03,281
If it's about the fire,

352
00:22:03,282 --> 00:22:04,907
we have nothing more to say.

353
00:22:04,908 --> 00:22:06,243
Oh, it's not about that.

354
00:22:07,119 --> 00:22:09,079
You know Jang Hee-ju, right?

355
00:22:12,416 --> 00:22:13,166
Yes.

356
00:22:13,709 --> 00:22:16,545
You were with Jang Hee-ju all night
at the real estate office, right?

357
00:22:17,254 --> 00:22:19,339
T-that's right.

358
00:22:19,798 --> 00:22:20,966
What did you two do when you met?

359
00:22:23,719 --> 00:22:24,678
Uh...

360
00:22:25,178 --> 00:22:28,931
We talked about the redevelopment project
and had drinks.

361
00:22:28,932 --> 00:22:30,183
- Hmm...
- And?

362
00:22:31,435 --> 00:22:35,438
I drank too much and fell asleep,

363
00:22:35,439 --> 00:22:37,690
and you came to pick me up
the next day, right?

364
00:22:37,691 --> 00:22:39,025
- Yes, that's right.
- Yes.

365
00:22:39,026 --> 00:22:42,612
Well, you came out
and took me home.

366
00:22:42,613 --> 00:22:43,488
Yes.

367
00:22:44,489 --> 00:22:46,992
And Ms. Jang Hee-ju
got in the car and drove away immediately.

368
00:22:47,701 --> 00:22:48,826
Yes, that's right.

369
00:22:48,827 --> 00:22:51,371
Hee-ju dropped me off
in front of my house.

370
00:22:51,914 --> 00:22:55,082
But when I checked where Jang Hee-ju
was headed through CCTV,

371
00:22:55,083 --> 00:22:56,877
you were being carried into your home.

372
00:22:58,670 --> 00:22:59,754
Yes.

373
00:22:59,755 --> 00:23:00,505
That's right.

374
00:23:01,381 --> 00:23:02,257
I have

375
00:23:03,175 --> 00:23:04,384
narcolepsy.

376
00:23:04,593 --> 00:23:05,259
Narcolepsy?

377
00:23:05,260 --> 00:23:08,596
My wife has some issues
like that with narcolepsy.

378
00:23:08,597 --> 00:23:11,390
Yes, I've been
so stressed out lately,

379
00:23:11,391 --> 00:23:12,893
and sometimes I have symptoms like that.

380
00:23:13,352 --> 00:23:14,602
With the redevelopment
project and whatnot,

381
00:23:14,603 --> 00:23:17,813
my kid is also preparing
for her entrance exams right now,

382
00:23:17,814 --> 00:23:18,981
so there's been a lot of stress.

383
00:23:18,982 --> 00:23:19,858
Yes.

384
00:23:21,735 --> 00:23:23,320
But you said you fell asleep.

385
00:23:23,779 --> 00:23:25,822
How do you know about
getting dropped off at home?

386
00:23:27,741 --> 00:23:29,534
You told me, right?

387
00:23:30,285 --> 00:23:31,119
Yes.

388
00:23:32,287 --> 00:23:34,538
So, Hee-ju helped out a lot.

389
00:23:34,539 --> 00:23:36,165
That's right.
Hee-ju worked hard.

390
00:23:36,166 --> 00:23:37,459
She helped out a lot.

391
00:23:42,130 --> 00:23:44,132
Was there no mention of her
going anywhere?

392
00:23:44,967 --> 00:23:47,426
She probably went
to the redevelopment site.

393
00:23:47,427 --> 00:23:50,514
Lately, that's all
she can think about.

394
00:23:55,686 --> 00:23:56,894
I tracked down the vehicle path.

395
00:23:56,895 --> 00:23:59,021
Jang Hee-ju visited Gi Su-jong's home,

396
00:23:59,022 --> 00:24:00,648
then went straight
to the redevelopment site.

397
00:24:00,649 --> 00:24:02,234
I haven't confirmed anything beyond that.

398
00:24:06,655 --> 00:24:07,989
That's it for now.

399
00:24:07,990 --> 00:24:09,408
No other unusual things?

400
00:24:09,658 --> 00:24:11,618
No, not really.

401
00:24:12,369 --> 00:24:13,452
I'm sorry but

402
00:24:13,453 --> 00:24:14,955
may I ask what happened?

403
00:24:15,956 --> 00:24:17,791
Jang Hee-ju was found dead.

404
00:24:18,625 --> 00:24:22,253
Well, we're still investigating,
so I can't share too much.

405
00:24:22,254 --> 00:24:24,089
There's a high chance she was murdered.

406
00:24:25,257 --> 00:24:26,216
What?

407
00:24:27,342 --> 00:24:28,135
But,

408
00:24:28,552 --> 00:24:29,553
I mean...

409
00:24:30,303 --> 00:24:32,305
How could that happen?

410
00:24:32,723 --> 00:24:34,057
I told you, right?

411
00:24:34,641 --> 00:24:36,475
I don't think Kim Gyun's death

412
00:24:36,476 --> 00:24:37,936
was just a mere hit-and-run.

413
00:24:38,937 --> 00:24:40,187
So, for you two,

414
00:24:40,188 --> 00:24:41,857
if anything comes to mind,
please contact me.

415
00:24:49,489 --> 00:24:51,241
Jeez...

416
00:24:52,034 --> 00:24:54,244
Seon, don't you think narcolepsy
is a bit far-fetched?

417
00:24:55,454 --> 00:24:57,121
Well, then what should I say?

418
00:24:57,122 --> 00:24:58,373
There are a lot of those people lately.

419
00:24:59,791 --> 00:25:03,252
But since Gyun was brought up...

420
00:25:03,253 --> 00:25:04,755
Hold on, what is this?

421
00:25:05,881 --> 00:25:07,424
Is that Mr. Nam?
Why is he calling?

422
00:25:07,841 --> 00:25:08,382
Hold on.

423
00:25:08,383 --> 00:25:09,592
Yes, Mr. Nam?

424
00:25:09,593 --> 00:25:10,886
Yes, my partner.

425
00:25:11,720 --> 00:25:14,389
I need to see you urgently.

426
00:25:15,724 --> 00:25:17,434
Oh, what's going on?

427
00:25:19,144 --> 00:25:21,396
You know Jang Hee-ju, right?

428
00:25:22,147 --> 00:25:23,940
I have something to discuss about her.

429
00:25:24,733 --> 00:25:29,696
Hmm, it seems our partner
is in a bit of trouble.

430
00:25:30,322 --> 00:25:32,532
What do you mean by that?

431
00:25:33,742 --> 00:25:35,618
Hey, let's skip the small talk.

432
00:25:35,619 --> 00:25:38,038
Try to hurry over here.

433
00:25:38,538 --> 00:25:40,123
I'll send you the address.

434
00:25:41,458 --> 00:25:44,794
And please
don't mention this to anyone.

435
00:25:44,795 --> 00:25:47,672
This is all for my partner's protection.

436
00:25:48,548 --> 00:25:49,800
- Got it?
- Yes.

437
00:25:50,884 --> 00:25:51,843
Okay, see you.

438
00:25:53,512 --> 00:25:54,721
What? What is it?

439
00:25:55,097 --> 00:25:57,224
Mr. Nam said
he wants to see me all of a sudden.

440
00:25:57,516 --> 00:25:59,476
I'll be right back, honey.

441
00:26:05,690 --> 00:26:08,193
No. 6458, 6458...

442
00:26:09,236 --> 00:26:09,819
Where's the car?

443
00:26:09,820 --> 00:26:11,655
- Huh? Not here yet.
- Okay.

444
00:26:12,155 --> 00:26:13,532
Did anything come up
with Gi Su-jong?

445
00:26:14,241 --> 00:26:16,409
It feels like he's lying,
but I'm not sure.

446
00:26:18,453 --> 00:26:21,705
No. 6458, 6458...

447
00:26:21,706 --> 00:26:22,457
Ju-ran.

448
00:26:24,292 --> 00:26:25,459
I think I found it.

449
00:26:25,460 --> 00:26:26,252
Let's see.

450
00:26:26,253 --> 00:26:27,546
No. 6458

451
00:26:27,838 --> 00:26:29,339
286-Teo-6458.

452
00:26:34,553 --> 00:26:35,387
Bo-ram.

453
00:26:36,096 --> 00:26:38,055
Oh, thanks.

454
00:26:38,056 --> 00:26:39,766
- Secure the memory card first.
- Sure.

455
00:26:47,315 --> 00:26:52,404
LEEUM BUILDING

456
00:26:54,197 --> 00:26:56,616
338 Sejeong-ro, Yongdaemun-gu, Seoul
Leeum Building

457
00:27:06,668 --> 00:27:08,086
Oh, you're here.

458
00:27:09,796 --> 00:27:11,422
Even in broad daylight,

459
00:27:11,423 --> 00:27:12,757
it feels a bit eerie, right?

460
00:27:13,508 --> 00:27:15,677
I've been all over the place,
doing government work.

461
00:27:16,052 --> 00:27:18,763
Reconstruction sites
are usually like this.

462
00:27:19,514 --> 00:27:22,559
Dark and damp with desolate moments.

463
00:27:23,101 --> 00:27:24,686
We have to endure these times

464
00:27:25,312 --> 00:27:26,730
for a bright new day to come.

465
00:27:27,689 --> 00:27:28,523
Got it?

466
00:27:28,857 --> 00:27:30,357
What are you doing? Come here.

467
00:27:30,358 --> 00:27:31,693
Read this for me.

468
00:27:36,823 --> 00:27:37,782
What's this?

469
00:27:38,450 --> 00:27:39,451
It's something fun.

470
00:27:39,826 --> 00:27:41,077
I wrote it myself.

471
00:27:52,923 --> 00:27:53,881
What are you waiting for?

472
00:27:53,882 --> 00:27:54,883
Hurry up and read it.

473
00:27:56,593 --> 00:27:58,385
"I confess the crime I have committed."

474
00:27:58,386 --> 00:28:00,429
"Due to business issues,
we had disagreements and during a dispute"

475
00:28:00,430 --> 00:28:03,225
"I unintentionally killed Jang Hee-ju
and disposed of the body."

476
00:28:07,687 --> 00:28:09,396
"I apologize for causing social discord."

477
00:28:09,397 --> 00:28:10,773
"I can't face my family."

478
00:28:10,774 --> 00:28:13,776
"With no place to run or road left
to take, I want to end everything here."

479
00:28:13,777 --> 00:28:16,320
"I'll bear all these sins
and punishments."

480
00:28:16,321 --> 00:28:17,072
What's this?

481
00:28:18,323 --> 00:28:19,199
That's right.

482
00:28:19,908 --> 00:28:20,951
It's your will.

483
00:28:21,576 --> 00:28:22,618
What do you think?

484
00:28:22,619 --> 00:28:23,453
Nice and neat.

485
00:28:24,079 --> 00:28:25,497
Not too emotional either.

486
00:28:25,830 --> 00:28:28,583
Just sign your name down there, okay?

487
00:28:50,522 --> 00:28:51,523
Jang Hee-ju.

488
00:28:53,066 --> 00:28:54,526
She's turning off the dash cam.

489
00:28:55,860 --> 00:28:56,778
Why is that?

490
00:28:58,488 --> 00:28:59,572
Check the recording
from the day before.

491
00:29:06,162 --> 00:29:07,455
It's Jang Hee-ju and Gi Su-jong.

492
00:29:16,923 --> 00:29:17,632
Huh?

493
00:29:18,425 --> 00:29:19,467
This person...

494
00:29:20,135 --> 00:29:21,511
Nam Sang-ho?

495
00:29:24,347 --> 00:29:25,807
You're ignoring my calls?

496
00:29:38,737 --> 00:29:39,946
What the hell?

497
00:29:41,573 --> 00:29:42,531
I got you.

498
00:29:42,532 --> 00:29:43,532
So what is this?

499
00:29:43,533 --> 00:29:46,745
You two just want to ditch me
and do it all, right?

500
00:29:50,373 --> 00:29:52,000
You're too loud.
Let's talk outside.

501
00:29:52,917 --> 00:29:55,002
Go out, go out.

502
00:29:55,003 --> 00:29:55,545
Go out.

503
00:29:59,632 --> 00:30:00,467
What's your deal?

504
00:30:01,718 --> 00:30:04,053
Were you ignoring my calls

505
00:30:04,054 --> 00:30:05,764
to run off with that jerk?

506
00:30:06,556 --> 00:30:08,975
Why would I do that?

507
00:30:09,893 --> 00:30:13,187
And do you really have
the right to say that,

508
00:30:13,188 --> 00:30:14,397
being a married man?

509
00:30:15,023 --> 00:30:17,358
You said it was better
that I'm a married man.

510
00:30:17,359 --> 00:30:19,276
What was that?

511
00:30:19,277 --> 00:30:20,486
Being relaxed

512
00:30:20,487 --> 00:30:21,738
and not being too fixated.

513
00:30:23,448 --> 00:30:25,617
That's just talk.

514
00:30:26,326 --> 00:30:30,455
You got to squeeze out some positives.

515
00:30:31,414 --> 00:30:32,665
Don't you have a conscience?

516
00:30:35,251 --> 00:30:37,379
I may be something, but so are you.

517
00:30:38,505 --> 00:30:41,216
Whether I meet another guy
or not, what's it to you?

518
00:30:42,342 --> 00:30:44,386
You don't really like that guy either.

519
00:30:45,053 --> 00:30:48,222
This is just a ploy
to grab his share.

520
00:30:48,223 --> 00:30:49,391
Isn't that right?

521
00:30:50,058 --> 00:30:53,352
You're not giving me what you promised,
Mr. Nam Sang-ho.

522
00:30:53,353 --> 00:30:56,563
I've done my part too.
Don't I deserve to get what I'm owed?

523
00:30:56,564 --> 00:30:58,858
If you wait, I'll give it to you.

524
00:30:59,275 --> 00:31:00,819
Why can't you trust people?

525
00:31:02,153 --> 00:31:04,988
We're almost there,
so just wait a little longer.

526
00:31:04,989 --> 00:31:06,323
I promise, okay?

527
00:31:06,324 --> 00:31:07,450
Oh, enough already.

528
00:31:08,284 --> 00:31:10,452
How many promises must you break?

529
00:31:10,453 --> 00:31:11,413
I don't need it.

530
00:31:12,247 --> 00:31:13,748
I'll handle it myself.

531
00:31:14,707 --> 00:31:15,542
You?

532
00:31:17,085 --> 00:31:19,044
You know I can ruin your life

533
00:31:19,045 --> 00:31:20,755
if I feel like it, right?

534
00:31:21,965 --> 00:31:24,134
With corruption and affairs,

535
00:31:25,343 --> 00:31:26,719
who should I tell?

536
00:31:27,512 --> 00:31:28,596
A congressman?

537
00:31:29,347 --> 00:31:30,306
Your wife?

538
00:31:31,724 --> 00:31:33,143
Before I expose everything,

539
00:31:33,726 --> 00:31:34,727
go home.

540
00:31:36,479 --> 00:31:37,188
Hey.

541
00:31:38,481 --> 00:31:41,568
Are you serious about that?

542
00:31:42,444 --> 00:31:43,485
I...

543
00:31:43,486 --> 00:31:44,696
I brought...

544
00:31:46,156 --> 00:31:48,283
some tteokbokki to share with you.

545
00:31:52,620 --> 00:31:54,247
What is this?

546
00:31:55,123 --> 00:31:57,750
This isn't child's play!

547
00:31:58,585 --> 00:32:02,045
That's why you're stuck working
under some old guy your whole life.

548
00:32:02,046 --> 00:32:04,423
You think you've made it? Get real.

549
00:32:04,424 --> 00:32:07,469
Sang-ho, I'll give you some pocket money.

550
00:32:08,011 --> 00:32:10,472
Take this and have fun with your wife.

551
00:32:10,722 --> 00:32:11,972
Oh, right.

552
00:32:11,973 --> 00:32:15,351
Wasn't it that your wife wasn't satisfied?

553
00:32:16,352 --> 00:32:17,187
Actually,

554
00:32:17,604 --> 00:32:19,062
I felt that way too.

555
00:32:19,063 --> 00:32:22,025
That's just too bad.

556
00:32:22,233 --> 00:32:23,318
Damn it.

557
00:32:26,613 --> 00:32:27,447
You...

558
00:32:34,579 --> 00:32:35,662
Hee-ju!

559
00:32:35,663 --> 00:32:36,998
Jang Hee-ju, wake up!

560
00:32:46,216 --> 00:32:47,717
Hey, it's me.

561
00:32:51,262 --> 00:32:53,223
I think you need to hurry
and come here quickly.

562
00:32:54,724 --> 00:32:57,519
So it was you who killed Hee-ju.

563
00:32:58,978 --> 00:32:59,771
Is that so?

564
00:33:01,147 --> 00:33:02,439
I know, right?

565
00:33:02,440 --> 00:33:05,151
Why was she so greedy about shares?

566
00:33:05,818 --> 00:33:08,153
She could've just taken
what she was given.

567
00:33:08,154 --> 00:33:10,323
But hey, at least it ends cleanly.

568
00:33:11,616 --> 00:33:16,454
Reflect on your sins and commit suicide
at the redevelopment site.

569
00:33:17,121 --> 00:33:18,164
Yes!

570
00:33:22,627 --> 00:33:23,628
What are you doing right now?

571
00:33:24,128 --> 00:33:25,755
How are you feeling right now?

572
00:33:26,756 --> 00:33:27,465
What?

573
00:33:28,258 --> 00:33:30,885
Is there something you want to say
to your family?

574
00:33:31,970 --> 00:33:32,887
Nothing?

575
00:33:34,847 --> 00:33:37,141
I guess not.
I really wanted to pass it on.

576
00:33:39,435 --> 00:33:40,520
Are you really going to shoot that?

577
00:33:48,111 --> 00:33:49,320
Ah!

578
00:33:51,322 --> 00:33:52,823
Damn it!

579
00:33:52,824 --> 00:33:53,783
Are you crazy?

580
00:33:54,409 --> 00:33:55,994
Why did you shoot me? That guy...

581
00:33:57,161 --> 00:33:58,913
- What should we do?
- What?

582
00:33:59,747 --> 00:34:02,417
This tteokbokki punk,
should I kill him or not?

583
00:34:03,793 --> 00:34:05,752
Hold on a second, Mr. Gi...

584
00:34:05,753 --> 00:34:07,171
S-Su-jong...

585
00:34:07,422 --> 00:34:10,008
We were getting
along well, right?

586
00:34:11,384 --> 00:34:13,845
We can make a lot of money soon!

587
00:34:14,387 --> 00:34:16,723
Why are we doing this?
Let's work together, Su-jong...

588
00:34:18,933 --> 00:34:20,184
I-I'll beg to you.

589
00:34:20,685 --> 00:34:21,603
Just spare my life.

590
00:34:21,936 --> 00:34:24,146
Just spare my life and

591
00:34:24,147 --> 00:34:26,773
I'll admit I killed Hee-ju.

592
00:34:26,774 --> 00:34:28,609
And if you kill me now,

593
00:34:28,610 --> 00:34:29,902
there's no evidence left!

594
00:34:30,570 --> 00:34:34,157
Our business would be ruined!

595
00:34:35,533 --> 00:34:37,619
How is there no evidence? There is.

596
00:34:38,745 --> 00:34:40,746
You said you deleted all the CCTV footage.

597
00:34:40,747 --> 00:34:42,582
Oh, I kept the important stuff.

598
00:35:11,110 --> 00:35:13,362
DELETE ONE FILE?

599
00:35:13,363 --> 00:35:14,739
DELETING FILE...

600
00:35:19,285 --> 00:35:19,952
Huh?

601
00:35:22,830 --> 00:35:24,791
It looks like
Nam Sang-ho is the culprit.

602
00:35:25,291 --> 00:35:27,042
Issue a manhunt on Nam Sang-ho
and track him down.

603
00:35:27,043 --> 00:35:27,835
Got it.

604
00:35:30,129 --> 00:35:31,963
Look here.

605
00:35:31,964 --> 00:35:33,465
If you let me die like this,

606
00:35:33,466 --> 00:35:36,177
do you think your headquarters
will just sit back?

607
00:35:36,552 --> 00:35:37,512
Clear this up right now.

608
00:35:38,054 --> 00:35:39,805
If you stop here,

609
00:35:39,806 --> 00:35:41,683
I'll put in a good word to Real Capital.

610
00:35:42,725 --> 00:35:44,519
It's not me that's doing the killing.

611
00:35:45,186 --> 00:35:46,396
It's suicide.

612
00:35:49,357 --> 00:35:51,567
Why are you doing this to me?

613
00:35:52,485 --> 00:35:53,486
I don't know.

614
00:35:53,861 --> 00:35:55,530
Let's say it's abuse of power.

615
00:35:56,155 --> 00:35:57,949
What?

616
00:36:00,451 --> 00:36:01,744
You're now the one in charge.

617
00:36:03,246 --> 00:36:04,163
Well then,

618
00:36:04,539 --> 00:36:05,540
did you make a decision?

619
00:36:06,541 --> 00:36:07,709
You should get revenge.

620
00:36:08,626 --> 00:36:10,210
Su-jong...

621
00:36:10,211 --> 00:36:11,087
Please...

622
00:36:13,673 --> 00:36:14,590
Let him live.

623
00:36:16,342 --> 00:36:17,050
What?

624
00:36:17,051 --> 00:36:17,802
I mean,

625
00:36:18,720 --> 00:36:20,096
let's do it by the book.

626
00:36:22,682 --> 00:36:24,767
But if we do it by the book, you'll die.

627
00:36:27,019 --> 00:36:29,272
I'll handle that on my own,

628
00:36:30,189 --> 00:36:31,399
so let's do it by the book.

629
00:36:34,485 --> 00:36:36,320
Jeez, this is no fun.

630
00:36:39,323 --> 00:36:40,283
Anyway,

631
00:36:41,075 --> 00:36:42,326
you're such a weird person.

632
00:36:50,084 --> 00:36:50,918
My mistake.

633
00:37:01,804 --> 00:37:02,763
I don't think Kim Gyun's death

634
00:37:02,764 --> 00:37:05,057
was just a mere hit-and-run.

635
00:37:05,266 --> 00:37:06,808
But you don't know this,
do you?

636
00:37:06,809 --> 00:37:08,853
Su-jong's connection to Gyun's death.

637
00:37:21,657 --> 00:37:23,117
KIM GYUN

638
00:37:40,551 --> 00:37:41,677
Gyun's birthday.

639
00:37:43,179 --> 00:37:44,555
It's 0314.

640
00:37:46,349 --> 00:37:47,683
INCORRECT PASSWORD ENTERED

641
00:37:48,059 --> 00:37:50,645
Mom's memorial day? Let's try 0630.

642
00:37:52,021 --> 00:37:52,814
INCORRECT PASSWORD ENTERED

643
00:38:12,458 --> 00:38:13,584
Da-rae's birthday.

644
00:38:21,384 --> 00:38:22,176
I did it.

645
00:38:29,433 --> 00:38:31,018
Real Capital
Nam Sang-ho's Slush Fund Records

646
00:38:34,355 --> 00:38:37,942
NAM SANG-HO'S SLUSH FUND TRANSFERS

647
00:38:44,490 --> 00:38:45,283
SEJEONG-RO REDEVELOPMENT INFORMATION

648
00:38:46,284 --> 00:38:46,993
SLUSH FUND RECORDS

649
00:38:58,421 --> 00:38:59,922
COMMERCIAL LEASE AGREEMENT

650
00:39:08,890 --> 00:39:09,807
GI SU-JONG'S FAMILY INFORMATION

651
00:39:12,768 --> 00:39:15,104
POLICE RECORDS NAME: KIM GYUN

652
00:39:43,090 --> 00:39:44,634
Oh, Da-rae.

653
00:39:46,302 --> 00:39:49,054
Where did you go earlier?

654
00:39:49,055 --> 00:39:52,642
Did you and Dad do something wrong again?

655
00:39:52,850 --> 00:39:54,434
No.

656
00:39:54,435 --> 00:39:55,353
I told you

657
00:39:56,354 --> 00:39:57,897
if there's something wrong,

658
00:39:58,773 --> 00:40:00,691
Mom will fix it.

659
00:40:11,118 --> 00:40:14,789
Remember what I said last time?

660
00:40:18,292 --> 00:40:19,168
Yes.

661
00:40:21,337 --> 00:40:26,133
That... wasn't how I truly felt.

662
00:40:29,303 --> 00:40:31,597
I was too harsh.

663
00:40:36,018 --> 00:40:37,061
Da-rae.

664
00:40:39,230 --> 00:40:41,523
I'll be back shortly.

665
00:40:41,524 --> 00:40:42,274
Okay.

666
00:40:58,624 --> 00:41:01,210
KIM GYUN

667
00:41:27,820 --> 00:41:30,031
LAST WILL

668
00:41:36,370 --> 00:41:37,163
Hey,

669
00:41:38,956 --> 00:41:40,207
are you going to kill me too?

670
00:41:43,002 --> 00:41:45,504
Am I some kind of serial killer?

671
00:41:45,880 --> 00:41:48,048
You're treating someone
who helped you as if they're a psycho.

672
00:41:48,049 --> 00:41:49,175
That's disappointing.

673
00:41:50,259 --> 00:41:52,136
You call this helping?

674
00:41:55,973 --> 00:41:59,643
We just need to keep moving
our remaining projects forward.

675
00:42:02,188 --> 00:42:03,980
You know, the 30 billion?

676
00:42:03,981 --> 00:42:04,857
We have to earn that.

677
00:42:05,399 --> 00:42:08,486
So, what are we going to do?

678
00:42:08,986 --> 00:42:11,572
What do you mean?
We have to deal with it.

679
00:42:12,239 --> 00:42:13,616
Deal with what?

680
00:42:13,949 --> 00:42:16,118
Well,

681
00:42:16,786 --> 00:42:18,204
who was that Pyeong-buk Gwan lady?

682
00:42:18,537 --> 00:42:19,287
Jeon Yi-gyeong.

683
00:42:19,288 --> 00:42:20,039
Right.

684
00:42:21,207 --> 00:42:22,249
Jeon Yi-gyeong.

685
00:42:23,167 --> 00:42:26,586
If that woman is gone,
Pyeong-buk Gwan will be resolved.

686
00:42:26,587 --> 00:42:28,798
Hey, are we just
going to kill people first?

687
00:42:29,090 --> 00:42:30,758
Come on, don't do that.

688
00:42:31,634 --> 00:42:34,260
I'll handle Jeon Yi-gyeong my way, okay?

689
00:42:34,261 --> 00:42:35,387
Stay out of it.

690
00:42:35,554 --> 00:42:37,807
What are you talking about?
I helped since you asked.

691
00:42:39,600 --> 00:42:40,643
Mister.

692
00:42:43,020 --> 00:42:44,605
Just stay still

693
00:42:45,397 --> 00:42:46,816
and do what you're told.

694
00:42:51,737 --> 00:42:53,030
Let's go with the flow.

695
00:42:53,656 --> 00:42:54,490
Okay?

696
00:42:57,535 --> 00:42:58,618
Are we all done?

697
00:42:58,619 --> 00:42:59,954
Yes, shall we go?

698
00:43:01,163 --> 00:43:02,331
See you again.

699
00:43:37,741 --> 00:43:39,577
You know me, right?

700
00:43:47,918 --> 00:43:50,045
I guess we never really talked.

701
00:43:53,132 --> 00:43:54,717
It must be hard for you.

702
00:43:55,342 --> 00:43:56,427
What brings you here?

703
00:44:06,103 --> 00:44:08,230
Have you met Aunt Yi-gyeong?
How is she doing?

704
00:44:09,773 --> 00:44:11,942
Oh, she's recovering.

705
00:44:12,568 --> 00:44:15,404
But the problem is
what's inside rather that the surface.

706
00:44:15,821 --> 00:44:17,656
The wounds in the heart

707
00:44:18,490 --> 00:44:20,367
can't be treated in the hospital.

708
00:44:24,788 --> 00:44:26,456
Yi-gyeong

709
00:44:26,457 --> 00:44:27,791
wants to see you.

710
00:44:28,209 --> 00:44:29,668
She feels sorry for you.

711
00:44:40,554 --> 00:44:43,098
That won't ease your heart.

712
00:44:43,474 --> 00:44:45,851
It will only hurt more people.

713
00:44:48,270 --> 00:44:50,522
Yi-gyeong has to overcome this herself.

714
00:44:51,649 --> 00:44:53,067
You can't hurt others

715
00:44:53,651 --> 00:44:55,486
because of your own wounds.

716
00:45:03,661 --> 00:45:06,288
Then what should we do?
How can we heal her heart?

717
00:45:08,374 --> 00:45:09,583
The time will come.

718
00:45:10,459 --> 00:45:14,421
There will come a time
when you can tell Yi-gyeong everything.

719
00:45:22,054 --> 00:45:24,765
WHEN? WHAT IF IT'S TOO LATE?

720
00:45:25,307 --> 00:45:27,685
You need to work to prevent that.

721
00:45:39,655 --> 00:45:41,949
BUT WHAT BRINGS YOU HERE, MR. KIM?

722
00:45:43,784 --> 00:45:44,994
I had something to find.

723
00:45:45,786 --> 00:45:48,455
But it seems I won't need it anymore.

724
00:46:02,803 --> 00:46:04,346
Did you find my phone?

725
00:46:07,057 --> 00:46:09,101
All the evidence is in there.

726
00:46:09,810 --> 00:46:12,020
But why can't even the police find it?

727
00:46:12,021 --> 00:46:13,480
Did someone take it?

728
00:46:14,231 --> 00:46:15,899
You're good at resolving things like this.

729
00:46:16,400 --> 00:46:18,902
You used to deal with stuff
like this with my mom, right?

730
00:46:19,611 --> 00:46:20,446
Yi-gyeong,

731
00:46:21,905 --> 00:46:25,200
finding your phone
doesn't mean you'll be free.

732
00:46:26,410 --> 00:46:27,328
At least,

733
00:46:28,537 --> 00:46:31,332
I can ruin Gi Su-jong and Kim Seon.

734
00:46:32,833 --> 00:46:34,084
Is that what you want?

735
00:46:35,794 --> 00:46:37,046
Is that even a question?

736
00:46:37,796 --> 00:46:39,631
Do you know how I ended up like this?

737
00:46:40,257 --> 00:46:41,591
Honestly, Mr. Kim,

738
00:46:41,592 --> 00:46:43,052
whose side are you on?

739
00:46:45,846 --> 00:46:47,514
Visiting hours are over.

740
00:46:52,102 --> 00:46:53,062
Okay,

741
00:46:54,605 --> 00:46:57,524
I'll try my best.

742
00:46:57,816 --> 00:46:58,817
You need to do that.

743
00:47:00,194 --> 00:47:01,904
If you had gone with Mom,

744
00:47:02,821 --> 00:47:04,490
she wouldn't have
ended up that way.

745
00:47:21,799 --> 00:47:24,676
THE LATE KIM GYUN

746
00:47:33,519 --> 00:47:34,520
Hello?

747
00:47:35,521 --> 00:47:36,521
Where are you now?

748
00:47:36,522 --> 00:47:37,731
Why aren't you
answering the phone?

749
00:47:38,982 --> 00:47:41,025
Oh, I was busy. Why?

750
00:47:41,026 --> 00:47:42,277
Mr. Nam is the culprit.

751
00:47:43,237 --> 00:47:44,863
Nam Sang-ho, that guy?

752
00:47:45,489 --> 00:47:47,574
Yeah, that bastard killed Hee-ju

753
00:47:48,325 --> 00:47:50,034
and tried framing me.

754
00:47:50,035 --> 00:47:52,371
You remember what Hwal-sung
mentioned back then, right?

755
00:47:53,789 --> 00:47:54,873
So, what about Nam Sang-ho?

756
00:47:56,375 --> 00:47:57,459
Is anyone with you?

757
00:47:58,752 --> 00:47:59,753
No one is here.

758
00:48:00,587 --> 00:48:01,839
Nam Sang-ho is dead.

759
00:48:02,423 --> 00:48:03,297
What?

760
00:48:03,298 --> 00:48:05,174
Those Real Capital guys

761
00:48:05,175 --> 00:48:06,050
are no joke.

762
00:48:06,051 --> 00:48:07,594
Those guys are crazy.

763
00:48:07,886 --> 00:48:09,847
They seem to be pulling
the strings from behind.

764
00:48:10,222 --> 00:48:11,515
I came to see Yi-gyeong.

765
00:48:12,141 --> 00:48:14,435
I think those guys
are going to do something to her.

766
00:48:14,893 --> 00:48:17,812
Contact Da-rae and get home fast.

767
00:48:17,813 --> 00:48:18,814
Lock the doors well.

768
00:48:20,858 --> 00:48:22,109
By any chance...

769
00:48:24,027 --> 00:48:25,696
Did they killed Gyun too?

770
00:48:27,030 --> 00:48:28,949
Yes, I think so.

771
00:48:30,117 --> 00:48:31,785
You knew about that?

772
00:48:34,163 --> 00:48:34,997
Yes.

773
00:48:38,459 --> 00:48:40,210
Why didn't you tell me?

774
00:48:40,836 --> 00:48:42,129
I'm sorry.

775
00:48:43,005 --> 00:48:44,589
I thought if you knew,

776
00:48:44,590 --> 00:48:45,966
it probably wouldn't have been good.

777
00:48:46,258 --> 00:48:48,092
You're always like this.

778
00:48:48,093 --> 00:48:50,053
You should have told me from the start!

779
00:48:51,680 --> 00:48:52,556
I'm sorry.

780
00:48:53,807 --> 00:48:54,516
Hang up.

781
00:49:02,983 --> 00:49:03,817
Where are you?

782
00:49:08,989 --> 00:49:11,158
It's late, so hurry back home.

783
00:49:16,330 --> 00:49:18,540
I'M ALMOST HOME

784
00:49:23,587 --> 00:49:25,923
I'll be home soon, so stay put.

785
00:49:26,298 --> 00:49:27,549
Lock the doors well.

786
00:49:39,728 --> 00:49:41,271
So, what happened?

787
00:49:41,813 --> 00:49:44,483
A report came from the station
and the officer said he was like this.

788
00:49:45,984 --> 00:49:48,278
So he died while we were
checking the dash cam.

789
00:49:48,654 --> 00:49:50,321
This is certain.

790
00:49:50,322 --> 00:49:52,658
The homemade gun used for the suicide
and Nam Sang-ho's note.

791
00:49:57,621 --> 00:49:58,455
Wait a minute.

792
00:49:59,706 --> 00:50:01,832
If Mr. Nam killed Jang Hee-ju at night,

793
00:50:01,833 --> 00:50:03,710
who was the Jang Hee-ju
in the CCTV footage from the next day?

794
00:50:04,920 --> 00:50:06,338
She came out with the landlord couple.

795
00:50:07,673 --> 00:50:08,757
Who else could it be?

796
00:50:11,301 --> 00:50:12,468
What?

797
00:50:12,469 --> 00:50:13,595
The Seyoon Building landlord's wife?

798
00:50:14,429 --> 00:50:15,681
Really? Why?

799
00:50:19,351 --> 00:50:20,727
KIM SEON

800
00:50:22,229 --> 00:50:24,939
Yes, this is Koh Ju-ran
from Yongdaemun.

801
00:50:24,940 --> 00:50:26,650
I want to see you right now.

802
00:50:29,319 --> 00:50:30,695
That's great.

803
00:50:30,696 --> 00:50:31,822
I have a lot of questions too.

804
00:50:47,462 --> 00:50:48,255
Just a moment.

805
00:50:48,630 --> 00:50:49,590
You can't go in.

806
00:50:51,216 --> 00:50:53,217
I just want to check
if she's okay.

807
00:50:53,218 --> 00:50:54,218
It'll only take a second.

808
00:50:54,219 --> 00:50:55,554
Visiting hours are over.

809
00:50:57,598 --> 00:50:58,557
Is Jeon Yi-gyeong

810
00:50:59,141 --> 00:51:00,058
really okay inside?

811
00:51:00,225 --> 00:51:01,184
Who are you?

812
00:51:02,936 --> 00:51:03,687
I'm family.

813
00:51:04,021 --> 00:51:05,188
What exactly
is your relationship with her?

814
00:51:08,233 --> 00:51:10,359
Well, we're like a family.
It'll just take a second.

815
00:51:10,360 --> 00:51:12,988
Visiting hours are over.
Please come back tomorrow.

816
00:51:13,655 --> 00:51:15,365
She has taken a sedative
and fallen asleep.

817
00:51:20,495 --> 00:51:23,832
So, there are people
targeting Yi-gyeong?

818
00:51:24,082 --> 00:51:24,916
Yes.

819
00:51:25,417 --> 00:51:26,960
They're truly devilish people.

820
00:51:27,419 --> 00:51:28,544
But,

821
00:51:28,545 --> 00:51:30,047
aren't the police guarding her?

822
00:51:30,505 --> 00:51:31,548
That's true,

823
00:51:32,382 --> 00:51:34,760
but it feels a bit uneasy here.

824
00:51:37,596 --> 00:51:38,764
Yi-gyeong said

825
00:51:39,431 --> 00:51:41,475
you kidnapped her.

826
00:51:44,019 --> 00:51:45,145
Oh...

827
00:51:46,313 --> 00:51:49,733
If you're that worried,
then you should guard her yourself.

828
00:51:52,986 --> 00:51:55,280
It's been tough for me
after a few days in the hospital.

829
00:51:55,947 --> 00:51:57,573
I should rest a bit tonight.

830
00:51:57,574 --> 00:51:58,408
Yes.

831
00:52:23,392 --> 00:52:25,686
LAUNDRY ROOM

832
00:52:41,785 --> 00:52:44,162
I keep thinking of Gyun
a lot more than I thought I would.

833
00:52:45,288 --> 00:52:47,124
He was usually pretty blunt.

834
00:52:48,959 --> 00:52:50,252
Maybe it was different with his sister.

835
00:52:51,586 --> 00:52:52,462
No.

836
00:52:53,422 --> 00:52:56,174
He only hung out with my husband.
We were always bickering with each other.

837
00:52:58,844 --> 00:53:00,303
I should've treated him better
while he was alive.

838
00:53:02,222 --> 00:53:04,266
I hate having
these obvious regrets.

839
00:53:09,020 --> 00:53:10,981
We caught Jang Hee-ju's killer.

840
00:53:11,440 --> 00:53:13,650
But there are still
suspicious circumstances.

841
00:53:15,652 --> 00:53:17,904
We know you're having
a hard time because of us.

842
00:53:20,699 --> 00:53:22,409
It's just part of police work
to come up empty,

843
00:53:22,951 --> 00:53:24,619
but they'll be caught eventually.

844
00:53:25,412 --> 00:53:26,913
That's how crime works.

845
00:53:29,332 --> 00:53:31,376
The one who told me this was Gyun.

846
00:53:49,019 --> 00:53:50,896
BOND TRANSFER CONTRACT

847
00:53:54,691 --> 00:53:55,776
How did you get this?

848
00:53:56,151 --> 00:53:59,988
At the Real Capital office,
Gyun found a USB drive.

849
00:54:01,823 --> 00:54:03,741
It was password protected,
so I didn't know what was on it,

850
00:54:03,742 --> 00:54:05,577
but it turned out to be Da-rae's birthday.

851
00:54:08,914 --> 00:54:12,500
They are the ledgers connected
to Real Capital's corruption

852
00:54:12,501 --> 00:54:14,169
and criminal evidence.

853
00:54:14,961 --> 00:54:17,631
NAM SANG-HO'S AIDE'S SLUSH FUND RECORDS

854
00:54:18,924 --> 00:54:19,800
What about the USB drive?

855
00:54:22,135 --> 00:54:24,137
And I don't know who,

856
00:54:25,055 --> 00:54:26,723
but the corruption ledgers
also have police involved.

857
00:54:27,474 --> 00:54:29,142
It's the Yongdaemun police.

858
00:54:30,477 --> 00:54:31,561
You mean our colleagues?

859
00:54:32,479 --> 00:54:34,356
I'm only giving it to you because

860
00:54:34,981 --> 00:54:36,983
Gyun has a good eye for people.

861
00:54:38,944 --> 00:54:40,611
As for the USB drive,

862
00:54:40,612 --> 00:54:43,240
I'll keep it until we find out
the inside conspirators.

863
00:54:44,991 --> 00:54:47,077
And I'm not sure yet,

864
00:54:48,161 --> 00:54:50,413
but the Real Capital employees

865
00:54:51,873 --> 00:54:54,584
are also involved in murder and threats.

866
00:54:55,836 --> 00:54:58,129
Gyun is likely one of those victims too.

867
00:55:02,801 --> 00:55:04,718
I'll look into this,
based on the information.

868
00:55:04,719 --> 00:55:07,513
But this alone isn't enough.

869
00:55:07,514 --> 00:55:09,766
Those guys will try to escape somehow.

870
00:55:12,978 --> 00:55:14,229
And in that process,

871
00:55:15,188 --> 00:55:16,565
you could be in danger.

872
00:55:19,276 --> 00:55:20,819
Who knows what could happen,
so please be careful.

873
00:55:22,070 --> 00:55:24,155
Yes, you be careful too.

874
00:55:32,122 --> 00:55:36,125
SLUSH FUND TRANSFER DETAILS

875
00:55:36,126 --> 00:55:38,128
CONSULTATIVE ROAD / YONGDAEMUN

876
00:55:43,925 --> 00:55:44,800
Hello?

877
00:55:44,801 --> 00:55:46,469
Could you please check one thing for me?

878
00:55:47,053 --> 00:55:50,765
Nara Bank 3659-453151.

879
00:55:53,351 --> 00:55:56,354
Let me know whose account it is
as soon as you can. Thank you.

880
00:56:46,321 --> 00:56:47,322
Help...

881
00:57:21,898 --> 00:57:24,985
LAUNDRY ROOM

882
00:57:32,784 --> 00:57:33,910
Go in and get some rest.

883
00:57:35,453 --> 00:57:37,455
You arrived just in time.

884
00:57:37,956 --> 00:57:38,747
Good job.

885
00:57:38,748 --> 00:57:39,958
Take care.

886
00:58:03,857 --> 00:58:04,858
What's going on?

887
00:58:16,161 --> 00:58:19,122
LAUNDRY ROOM

888
00:58:33,219 --> 00:58:34,304
What's going on?

889
00:58:38,475 --> 00:58:39,184
You...

890
00:58:45,356 --> 00:58:47,107
Is that you, Su-jong?

891
00:58:47,108 --> 00:58:47,817
Yes.

892
00:59:13,134 --> 00:59:15,053
Yi-gyeong, just hang on a bit.

893
00:59:32,862 --> 00:59:33,780
Let's go.

894
00:59:49,629 --> 00:59:51,463
Hey, pull over!

895
00:59:51,464 --> 00:59:52,422
Stop right there!

896
00:59:52,423 --> 00:59:53,967
Entertainment expenses
related to Yongdaemun

897
00:59:54,759 --> 00:59:55,343
COSTS ASSOCIATED WITH YONGDAEMUN

898
01:00:01,349 --> 01:00:02,142
Yes?

899
01:00:03,768 --> 01:00:04,519
What?

900
01:00:05,019 --> 01:00:06,229
Jeon Yi-gyeong has disappeared?

901
01:00:07,814 --> 01:00:08,981
This is insane.

902
01:00:08,982 --> 01:00:10,483
Okay, I'm heading out now.

903
01:00:19,742 --> 01:00:20,535
Huh?

904
01:00:21,494 --> 01:00:22,787
What are you doing so late?

905
01:00:23,788 --> 01:00:24,747
Sergeant Keum?

906
01:00:25,290 --> 01:00:26,332
You haven't gone home yet?

907
01:00:26,499 --> 01:00:29,210
Oh, I heard from Detective Yoon
that you met Gyun's sister.

908
01:00:29,586 --> 01:00:31,462
- Oh...
- He said there was a tip.

909
01:00:32,255 --> 01:00:34,631
Oh, is that it?

910
01:00:34,632 --> 01:00:35,633
Oh.

911
01:00:36,634 --> 01:00:37,552
It's nothing.

912
01:00:37,677 --> 01:00:39,761
Come on, what is it?
Is it something juicy?

913
01:00:39,762 --> 01:00:41,346
It's really nothing.

914
01:00:41,347 --> 01:00:43,641
I'll let you know

915
01:00:44,350 --> 01:00:45,185
once I'm sure.

916
01:00:46,477 --> 01:00:48,313
Okay then.

917
01:00:51,316 --> 01:00:52,192
Yes.

918
01:00:56,654 --> 01:00:59,616
This account number belongs
to Sergeant Keum Yong-hoon

919
01:01:04,078 --> 01:01:05,955
I told you to stop poking around.

920
01:01:27,769 --> 01:01:34,359
KIM GYUN

921
01:02:01,302 --> 01:02:02,345
Ms. Kim Seon.

922
01:02:09,769 --> 01:02:11,187
Da-rae is sleeping.

923
01:02:13,856 --> 01:02:15,024
Oh, right.

924
01:02:16,359 --> 01:02:17,694
Da-rae can't hear, right?

925
01:02:20,905 --> 01:02:22,657
I heard you met with the police.

926
01:02:24,200 --> 01:02:25,118
How did it go?

927
01:02:25,868 --> 01:02:28,454
Did you manage to find justice?

928
01:02:31,582 --> 01:02:34,252
I came to get my things today.

929
01:02:35,336 --> 01:02:36,296
Where is it?

930
01:02:41,551 --> 01:02:42,593
I said, where is it?

931
01:02:44,721 --> 01:02:46,055
Can I take it today?

932
01:02:52,270 --> 01:02:53,688
GI SU-JONG

933
01:03:02,280 --> 01:03:04,282
SEON

934
01:03:09,537 --> 01:03:11,205
Seon, what's going on?

935
01:03:13,333 --> 01:03:14,458
SEONGive it to me.

936
01:03:14,459 --> 01:03:15,793
- Give me the phone.
- What are you doing?

937
01:03:16,002 --> 01:03:17,754
Give it to me.

938
01:03:19,047 --> 01:03:20,840
Oh my, Mr. Gi Su-jong.

939
01:03:21,841 --> 01:03:22,675
What's happening?

940
01:03:34,812 --> 01:03:36,813
SPECIAL THANKS TO ACTOR KIM EUI-SUNG

941
01:03:36,814 --> 01:03:38,857
SPECIAL THANKS TO ACTOR MIYAVI

942
01:03:38,858 --> 01:03:40,818
SPECIAL THANKS TO ACTOR PARK BYUNG-EUN

943
01:03:52,830 --> 01:03:55,916
MAD CONCRETE DREAMS

944
01:03:55,917 --> 01:03:56,708
Da-rae!

945
01:03:56,709 --> 01:03:59,086
Then, can you give up on the building?

946
01:03:59,087 --> 01:04:00,545
SEONFor our family,

947
01:04:00,546 --> 01:04:02,882
can you give up everything
and choose family?

948
01:04:03,132 --> 01:04:06,051
If you get divorced,
part of your share will go to your wife.

949
01:04:06,052 --> 01:04:08,553
Jeon Yi-gyeong wasn't the problem.
It was Kim Seon.

950
01:04:08,554 --> 01:04:10,181
I told you to stop poking around.

951
01:04:10,681 --> 01:04:12,140
You're just hopeless.

952
01:04:12,141 --> 01:04:13,517
You have
everything now, right?

953
01:04:13,518 --> 01:04:15,478
You cleared out all the obstacles.

954
01:04:15,728 --> 01:04:17,104
- I'm scared of you now.
- Seon!

955
01:04:17,105 --> 01:04:18,355
I can't do this.

956
01:04:18,356 --> 01:04:19,398
Let's get a divorce.

957
01:04:19,399 --> 01:04:21,566
Tell me. What's the problem?

958
01:04:21,567 --> 01:04:23,903
Can you kill my wife?

